# Everything the build produces for itself, so a local `dotnet build` or `vp build` cannot leak a
# host-shaped artifact into the image and cannot invalidate a layer by changing.
**/bin
**/obj
**/node_modules
**/dist
CodeExplorer/wwwroot
# `build.cs` stages the Windows zip here, and it is a whole publish output: uploading it as build
# context would cost more than the image build itself.
artifacts/

# Local state and tooling output: a developer's data directory holds clones, indexes and DuckDB spill
# files, and none of it is small.
data/
**/*.duckdb
**/*.duckdb.wal
TestResults/
.vite/
.vp/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local

# History, editors and the docs: the image build reads none of them, and .git alone is most of the
# context a plain `docker build` would otherwise upload.
.git
.github
.idea
.vs
docs/
*.md

# The test project. Nothing in the image runs it, and leaving it out keeps the restore to one project.
CodeExplorer.Tests/

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
